course: dictionary
lesson: 7630
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around the word: they are its clues. «Blender and food processor blades can cut deep into fingers in a split second.» Blender and blades are kitchen things, so a food processor must be a kitchen machine.
explain: Computing lessons use processor in a different way. The processor, or CPU (central processing unit), is the part of a computer that carries out instructions. «The processor, or CPU, is the chip that carries out the instructions; it gets hot when it works hard, so it usually sits under a fan.» Hot and fan are the clues that this is a computer part.
explain: Always test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "a kitchen machine that chops" in the food sentence and check it still makes sense. Try "a chip that carries out instructions" in the computer sentence. If your meaning does not fit, look for another one.
fact: A processor is the part of a computer that carries out instructions and does calculations.
fact: The processor is also called the CPU, which stands for central processing unit.
fact: A food processor is a kitchen machine that chops, mixes or blends food quickly.
fact: A processor can also be a company or machine that treats or changes materials.
fact: A faster processor makes a computer or phone quicker.
exercise: «Blender and food processor blades can cut deep into fingers in a split second.» In this sentence, what is a food processor? | A program for writing text | A computer chip that carries out instructions | A company that sells blenders | *A kitchen machine that chops, mixes or blends food quickly
exercise: The processor is also called the CPU. What does CPU stand for? | Computer program utility | *Central processing unit | Computer power and speed | Code and program update
exercise: «The processor gets hot when it works hard, so it usually sits under a fan.» In this sentence, what is the processor? | A program for writing text | *The chip in a computer that carries out instructions | A company that treats materials | A machine that cooks food
test: Mia says a word processor is a kitchen machine. Is she right? | Yes, it blends food | *No, it is a program for writing text | No, it is a company | Yes, it chops food quickly
test: What makes a computer or phone quicker, according to the lesson? | A louder speaker | A longer word | *A faster processor | A bigger fan
exam: A processor can also be which of these? | A computer chip that follows programs | A food you can chop | *A company or machine that treats or changes materials | A program for writing text
